{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467842-trying-to-find-computer-stats-owod","id":1467842,"title":"Trying to find Computer Stats (OWOD)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-14T17:43:38-08:00","id":1467842,"title":"Trying to find Computer Stats (OWOD)","content":"One of my players recently acquired an experimental computer from a corporate raid (through shenanigans). When he asked me what it could do for him in game terms, I said I'd get back to him. I'd thought in a gamebook I'd seen stats and benefits for hardware of various levels, but diving through my collection hasn't turned up much. I'd be happy for some help here!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T20:07:44-08:00","id":1467851,"title":"","content":"The only system in V20 is that the quality of the computer increases the difficulty to hack into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T20:20:14-08:00","id":1467853,"title":"","content":"Some older texts - player's guides, mostly - have more elaborate systems, but they're also a reminder that &quot;more elaborate&quot; does not necessarily mean &quot;better&quot;, unless you have the systems knowledge to, for example, make giving viruses Abilities a significant point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T23:00:35-08:00","id":1467858,"title":"","content":"Huh, wonder what I was thinking of. Like I could easily give him bonus dice to use the Computer, but I really thought there was a system for that. Well, having it be harder to hack is good too, but he was talking about breaking modern encryption easily with how many &quot;floating operations per second&quot; the computer could make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T21:04:34-08:00","id":1468223,"title":"","content":"In this day and age, &quot;experimental computer from a corporate raid&quot; generally means some tie to quantum computing. If this is the case, it could be interesting to browse some ideas in the web of things to do with this kind of device and keep the ones you find more interesting.<br /> <br /> Between things a quantum computer can actually do (reverse engineer quantum states), things it can probably do sometime in the near future (faster than light communication through information teleport), and things it can't do, but people think it can (teleport people, develop a conscience, rewrite reality Dr. Manhattan style), you could do worse than basing this thing in MtA to some extent (anything you feel comfortable with).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T23:22:54-08:00","id":1468236,"title":"","content":"Some ideas<br /> <br /> 1- It's made for a very specific reason. like accounting or producing music or simulating... submarine warfare. Someone might be interested in this. Consider point 4 if the player really wants to keep it.<br /> <br /> 2- It's a prototype that's simply more advanced than anything currently available but isn't overly futuristic. As a Vampire, if you went into torpor for a year or two, it'd be a normal consumer product. You may want to sell it to a competitor. If the vampire wants to keep it, it... loads faster.<br /> <br /> 3- Mage shenanigans. Read mage.<br /> <br /> 4- Vampire has rules for Fetishes (like in werewolf, objects possed by spirits) in these simplified rules, such an object can grant between 1-5 bonus die for the main thing that item uses. Otherwise you can open a copy of WTA and throw in some crazy powers from activation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T01:00:27-08:00","id":1468241,"title":"","content":"If it has a really good graphics editing suite, it may give a bonus in some crafts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T04:41:36-08:00","id":1468255,"title":"","content":"SELENE, an Exascale Computer, able to calculate 10 to the 18th power FLOPS (floating point operations per second). Though not an A.I., SELENE can run circles around any current Mortal technology.<br /> <br /> I know, cart before the horse, I didn't think the player could actually acquire it, but she did. Lesson to the student I guess, if you don't want something to be an option, don't let it be one. I could deny her the prize pretty easily (I considered that at first), but after all the effort that felt like I was being a bad Storyteller. Our compromise so far is that she agrees that hooking this thing up to the internet will let people find her, so she's mostly using it to compile programs, crunch data, and run codebreaking software.<br /> <br /> EDIT: as an aside, it's always made me wonder why Vampire has had Computers as a Knowledge from the very beginning, and later, Technology was added, yet VtM isn't really a game about hacking or advancements in technology (quite the reverse, since such things threaten the Masquerade) and hackers like Bobby Weatherbottom are treated as plot devices...yet especially in Revised, several Clanbooks had a &quot;hacker&quot; archetype presented and the Gangrel Clanbook especially pointed out that the internet was something the Clan would Embrace (pun intended). Yet the rules for programming and hacking were at best, bare bones.<br /> <br /> Maybe that's why the Nosferatu project failed, vampires are just bad hackers, lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","user":"Lynceus","date":". 11-18-2021, 07:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T08:11:22-08:00","id":1468272,"title":"","content":"Vampires excel pretty well with &quot;hacking&quot; but &quot;hacking&quot; in this context means tricking someone into giving their personal details or sneaking to someone's physical address and tampering with their things. As for writing Viruses and such, there are only so many hours in the night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T10:04:30-08:00","id":1468278,"title":"","content":"Vampire has Computers because it was written in 1991. This was before the home computing boom (largely pushed by the growing Internet boom) when the idea of having your own computer at home wasn't really &quot;normal&quot; yet. 30 years later most people have a more powerful and capable computer in their pocket than what was commonly sold in '91 to home users. The role and ubiquity of computers has change drastically in the past few decades; and Vampire didn't really age well in that regard. In the early 90s we knew computers were going to be important, so it was important to cover how good characters would be with them, even if the technology of the time didn't inspire the VtM authors into more detailed mechanics for the game (though Mage did get much increasingly more thorough ones.... but having a core Tradition be hackers necessitated that).<br /> <br /> Had Onyx Path gotten to make their idea for a new VtM edition, it's entirely possible Computers would have be removed from the game as an Ability (the CofD developers almost cut it from 2e but opted to keep it for consistency and facilitating programmer concepts). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T10:12:37-08:00","id":1468279,"title":"","content":"The problem is that modeling computer usage in RPGs has been a challenge since always, but one that most left by the wayside.<br /> <br /> Mage rules really aren't the worst call you can make here. It is not that you'll treat the computer as a Mage for all intents and purposes, but that those rules will give you more ideas on things to do, and a starting point for doing them.<br /> <br /> Other option is to treat individual programs or suites of programs as tools that allow or give a bonus to certain tasks, and the computer itself as a cap on how much of a bonus you can get out of it. The character then may customize the computer by acquiring or designing programs.<br /> <br /> You can look into other RPGs for ideas, but from the top of my head, the only one a remember with half-decent rules for computer using is Shadowrun, and that isn't an easy read, ever. Cyberpunk is moronic and I never understood all the hype around it, and I'm a fan of Neuromancer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T10:43:15-08:00","id":1468281,"title":"","content":"Ultimately, the larger problem for VtM here isn't the lack of in-depth computer rules, but the lack of any sort of basic equipment rules to adjudicate the differences between a $500 refurbished netbook, a high end gaming desktop, and a $1.2 billion supercomputer (the price tag on the current most powerful non-distributed computer that's actually an exascale computer even if only in limited functions and is &quot;just&quot; ~400-500 petaFLOPS in the most common generic performance tests).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T12:14:33-08:00","id":1468291,"title":"","content":"I personally think Schrecknet was a valid concept that should ave received at least half as much attention as the Virtual Adepts, even if just by porting rules and concepts.<br /> <br /> But indeed, the role of computers in VtM is still much informed by a time when then very idea of people gathering at a forum like this one was alien and would need a lot of specialized skills, not just from the backend providers but from everyone involved.<br /> <br /> So much so that we have an excellent example of how computers are in VtM by their display in Bloodlines, where we're stuck with reading e-mails at green screen terminals.<br /> <br /> And this complete lack of basic equipment rules, that instead of being corrected with time, just became a system legacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T16:13:54-08:00","id":1468307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467842-trying-to-find-computer-stats-owod?p=1468291#post1468291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But indeed, the role of computers in VtM is still much informed by a time when then very idea of people gathering at a forum like this one was alien and would need a lot of specialized skills, not just from the backend providers but from everyone involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>We had BBSes and Usenet in the old days, and forums like this one have been a staple since the late 90s. This is not cutting edge at all. Heck did you ever see an old Shadowrun book with the Shadwland posts and comments?<br /> <br /> Computers is still a valid skill. Just because people have a smartphone in their pocket and an app for everything doesn't mean they're really good at it. All a smartphone and an app would really help with is an additional dice or a difficutly break on certain checks and great access to information. You still need a skill to cover actual ripping computers apart and getting them to work, programming, networking or anything more complex than what someone's mum can do on her smartphone. Another approach would be to treat Technology like Crafts and insist that you need a specific area of technology to be good at.<br /> <br /> For a RPG like this one you don't even need that much more granularity, because really, we're in the land of &quot;HACK THE PLANET!&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T18:12:12-08:00","id":1468317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467842-trying-to-find-computer-stats-owod?p=1468307#post1468307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We had BBSes and Usenet in the old days, and forums like this one have been a staple since the late 90s.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm perfectly aware of that, that's not the point.<br /> <br /> Usenet and its precursors were still niche at the early 90's and demanded some skill to install, setup, run, find servers and use. Not a huge amount of skill for someone involved with computers, but alien to the more casual user. We're talking about a time when casual computer users weren't exactly a thing in the same sense of today.<br /> <br /> And I'm not promoting the elimination of the Computer skill. Quite the opposite, I fully agree that it is important and not that common. Indeed I totally disagree with the idea of removing it from the game.<br /> <br /> But VtM is still greatly informed by the role of computers at that time, with the added problem of not being a game meant to explore computers in detail. As I said, it is still a game that sees computers as they are shown in Bloodlines, where the skill's only actual use is to hack into weird green terminals with less complexity than an IBM 3270 to read txt files and short e-mails.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-19T00:27:15-08:00","id":1468333,"title":"","content":"I'm not even sure Computers is a knowledge by modern standards either. Most operating systems are so user friendly these days 5 year olds can use them. But that's neither here nor there. Another problem I foresee with &quot;hacking&quot; is no real standard for how hard it should be- major utilities, corporations, and even government agencies get information stolen from them or services denied all the time. And a lot of government agencies are kind of bad at this sort of thing. I recall reading about a state website that a simple right click and view source uncovered thousands of social security numbers and information, and when the reporter who discovered this major FUBAR reported it, the embarrassed governor sued him for &quot;hacking&quot;. I mean, we've all seen how strange dice rolls are, and with Merits like Computer Aptitude having been part of the game from the beginning, let alone the use of Disciplines to social network, let alone getting great insights from staring into a sea of code with Eyes of Chaos, it really seems to come down to &quot;what do you want to do?&quot;. 5 successes is usually &quot;best possible result&quot; for many things, but have I seen a guy roll Wits + Computers at a staggeringly high difficulty and get 10 successes? Sure I have, it happens. I know that the answer to all this is ultimately, &quot;what do I want to allow&quot; for my game. But I hate feeling like a character who invests in an Ability has to play &quot;Mother May I&quot; with the Storyteller. Even if I've had way more problems with people starting with Science 4 than I have with Brawl 5. &quot;Hyuk huk huk, I'm going to blow up the Toreador Primogen's Haven!&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-19T02:57:36-08:00","id":1468338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467842-trying-to-find-computer-stats-owod?p=1468333#post1468333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not even sure Computers is a knowledge by modern standards either.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sure is. You still can get far more from your computer by knowing what to do than by just going with the basic instructions. Yes, computers can do a lot more for common users now. But they also can do a lot more for advanced users.<br /> <br /> But this, again, highlights the problems with how the skill operates in VtM. The game really gives you little support on what to do with it. What I think we can do is brainstorm uses for the ability, so we have a more concrete grasp of the tasks it does. We'll also need rules for the computers themselves, something the game never cared about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-19T04:39:22-08:00","id":1468340,"title":"","content":"There's two main problems with Computers as an Ability at this point in time:<br /> <br /> 1) Computers are ubiquitous. Yes, this counts. Things that used to be taught regarding computers in graduate programs are now things most kids in developed countries learn in middle school if not earlier. Everything has a computer in it. My car is a computer. My kitchen is full of computers. My lawnmower is a computer. Operating a computer is no longer specialized training. Repairing computers is no longer specialized training. This means the vast majority of what Computers covered back in '91 doesn't have a place under a Computer Ability any more. And it's really simple why: you don't need to understand how they work to use them. One of the things that change significantly in the late 90s is that computers got easy enough to use that they're magic block boxes. You press buttons and stuff happens. Operations that used to take hours of training because you had to actually understand how the computer works to get it to do what you want has been reduced to, &quot;press this button.&quot;<br /> <br /> The easy of use really matters because it means that it doesn't make sense for a Computers Ability to gate your characters' actions when using a computerized tool. Writing a document in a word processor program is long past the point of needing enough dots in Computer to know how to use one. Now, people that don't write documents in a word processor are the weird ones, and Expression or Academics for actually knowing how to write effectively is what really matters. The folks that fix your car are going to be using a tablet to access diagnostics, and nobody expects them to be computer whizzes to do it.<br /> <br /> Computers have gone the way of lots of technology before them. The Science and Technology Abilities easily cover everything you need. <br /> <br /> 2) Computers as a game trait is not longer really important for facilitating concepts. One of the jobs of Abilities is to help embody the specifics of character concepts. Being the &quot;computer guy&quot; used to be a thing. Concepts around computers have evolved as our relationship to them has evolved. The social engineering aspect of cracking - which has always been there - is more prominent as things like identity theft become common crimes. IT departments aren't full of people with Masters degrees and PhDs, because they're not dealing with theoretical things. They're digital maintenance and security. A broader Ability like Technology better represents modern computer related concepts because integration and interaction between devices is a lot more central than coding skills.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}